  "script": {
    "hook": "Sounds like a maybe. Often means no. One polite business word, and what to do next.",
    "points": [
      "Picture a meeting. You pitch your idea, and the client says, けんとうします. That is, we will consider it.",
      "You hear, they are interested. But often, it is a gentle way to say no. Nobody loses face. Sometimes, though, they really do think it over.",
      "Watch what comes next. A real maybe has a date or a question. For example, けんとうして、きんようびまでにおへんじします. In English, I will think it over and reply by Friday."
    ],
    "takeaway": "If you hear nothing more, ask in a friendly way, いつごろおへんじをいただけますか. When can I hear back ?",
    "cta": "Send this to your study partner."
  },
